/E (An item on a bill may be chargedat a price different from the expected price. In such cases the total on the receipt no longer agrees with the individual lines. Identifying which item caused the difference requires comparing each line separately. BillBuster performs this comparison automatically and points to the exactitem that has caused the mismatch. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Receipts may contain duplicate items or values that look unusual compared with the rest of the bill. These may be genuine purchases or accidental entries. Detecting them manually is difficult, whereas a rule-based analysis can flag them consistently for the user to review. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (The BillBuster project was developedasa mini project during the internship in Data Analytics and Data Science. It demonstrates howdata extraction, cleaning, validation, and visualization can be combined into a single practicalapplication. The project focuses on transforming raw receipt images into reliable, structuredinformation. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Manual checking of receipts requires reading every line, adding the prices, and comparing the result with the printed total. Thisbecomes tiresome when many receipts are involved. Small errors such as a wrong price orarepeated item are easy to miss, especially when the receipt is long or the print is faint. Beforeautomation, a complete check of one receipt took around 120 seconds in the test comparison,which is not practical for regular use. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (The printed total of a receipt shouldequal the sum of its items plus tax, minus any discount. When it does not, the receipt is inconsistent. Such mismatches may be caused by billing errors, incorrect discounts, or by characters that were read wrongly during OCR. The application reports the receipt total, the sum of items, and the difference between them so that the reason can be investigated. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
