667 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (BillBuster, developed as a mini project during the Data Analytics and Data Science internship, provides an efficient and practical solution for analyzing bills and receipts. The application combines image capture, OCR using Pytesseract, regex-based entity extraction, rule-based validation, SQLite storage, and a Plotly dashboard into a single workflow. By using this pipeline, unstructured receipt images are transformed into structured data that can be verified and analyzed. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
668 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (The project helps identify errors such as item price mismatches, total discrepancies, duplicate items, and unusual values. In testing, the math rule validation reached 100% accuracy on 50 receipts, database operations completed in under 8 ms, and OCR precision reached 94.2% for clear prints and 76.5% for degraded prints, with the lower value triggering an audit flag. The average time for a complete audit was reduced from 120 seconds to 15 seconds. The Scan, Receipt Detail, Insights, and History screens make the results simple to understand and act upon. This project also gave practical experience in data cleaning, validation, analysis, visualization, and application development. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
669 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (The project can be further improved in the future. OCR accuracy can be increased by adding image preprocessing such as noise removal, deskewing, and contrast enhancement, or by using deep learning based OCR models. Machine learning models can be introduced for automatic category prediction and for detecting unusual spending. Support for multiple languages and currencies, and for different receipt layouts, would broaden the use of the application. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
670 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (Additional features such as cloud storage, user accounts, budget alerts, export of reports to Excel or PDF, integration with accounting tools, and a mobile application can make the system more useful. Automatic reminders for flagged receipts, warranty tracking, and integration with payment apps are further possibilities. These enhancements would improve the accuracy, usability, and scalability of the application. Overall, the project demonstrates how data analytics and OCR can be used to convert receipts into reliable insights and support better financial awareness and decision-making. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
671 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 175 0 R
/T (12. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE ENHANCEMENT )
/E (12. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE ENHANCEMENT )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
